comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T12:57:31.272Z",codex-agent,"Companion specification: pm-cli-website-zchz (read only). Local package only; release held for maintainer approval. Use native Knowledge items, registered fields, certified reads, host token estimation and process-safe memory mutation locking."
  "2026-10-19T13:08:07.483Z",codex-agent,"Implementation covers all seven commands and shared SDK entry points. Embedded SDK generic field writes require active extension registration; native registered schema options through client.run preserve in-process operation without extension recursion. Source copy remains private and external. Tests exercise real trackers, full host output and independent process recallers."
  "2026-10-19T13:24:52.194Z",codex-agent,"Packed distribution acceptance passed for both npm/npx and Bun/bunx: 2 tests passed. The first private-copy round trip imported 281 files and exported all 281 byte-identically; re-import reported 281 unchanged and zero writes. Final lexical ranking and native semantic edit safeguards are being rechecked before final acceptance."
  "2026-10-19T13:32:38.899Z",codex-agent,"All six feature-linked pm test commands passed. Baseline revert proof run after restoring all sources: 3 passed, zero failed. Production audit, duplication and docstrings are clean in preliminary checks. Full isolated npm and Bun release gates follow on the implementation commit."
  "2026-10-19T13:41:11.116Z",codex-agent,"Accepted private-copy aggregate: 281 imported; re-import 281 unchanged, zero created or updated; 281 exports byte-identical by recursive diff. Index 1498 of 1500 estimated tokens, 248 omitted. Recall token/reference-rank pairs in the requested query order: 759/1, 752/1, 751/omitted-from-three, 737/1, 738/3. Verification checked 280 facts: 198 stale, failing claims file=377 flag=249 symbol=34. Consolidation dry run: merge=0 supersedes=1 archive=189; no apply. Private scratch data removed."
  "2026-10-19T13:41:15.027Z",codex-agent,"Both isolated release gates passed on the completed implementation: npm run release:check and bun run release:check, each 12 stages, 79 unit/tooling tests and 2 packed consumers, zero failed. Coverage across all 19 authored source files: 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines (1440/1440 statements and lines, 673/673 branches, 72/72 functions). Docstrings 65 declarations; duplication zero; production vulnerabilities zero; 42 packed files all allowlisted. Fresh no-local clone: health 10 checks and validate 10 checks, zero warnings. Four behavioral revert proofs failed under reversion and passed after restoration."
  "2026-10-19T13:55:58.723Z",codex-agent,"Round two: conservative evidence classification across bounded repeated roots, frontmatter identity and alias links, compact ranked recall plus full get, aggregate privacy diagnostics, descriptive help and age-gated archival. Local-only work; synthetic regressions and private aggregate proof before both release gates."
  "2026-10-19T14:32:17.864Z",codex-agent,"Isolated npm release gate passed: 88 tests, 0 failures, 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across 19 configured source files, zero production vulnerabilities, zero duplication, 2 packed consumers accepted through npx and bunx including detailed import help, repeated verification roots, nested basename evidence and full get. Bun release gate pending. Linked round-two regression runner passed 9/9."
  "2026-10-19T14:38:35.200Z",codex-agent,"Both final release gates passed in isolated HOME/Git identity environments: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each ran 88 tests with zero failures/skips plus 2 packed npx/bunx consumers. Both report 100% statement, branch, function and line coverage across all 19 configured source files; zero production vulnerabilities; zero duplication; 42 allowlisted packed files. Three behavioral revert proofs and the 9/9 linked regression runner are recorded. All private proof artifacts deleted. Local-only review; no push or repository creation."
  "2026-10-19T15:52:22.211Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: verified all 17 unresolved threads at 3df1e75. Plan bounded in-process verification, raw-field privacy, semantic timestamps, recoverable consolidation, current atomic exports, attribution and regression proofs. No private source data is required."
  "2026-10-19T16:02:15.658Z",codex-agent,"Implemented all 17 thread fixes and both orchestrator findings. Verification streams indexed regular files with 64 MiB run and 8 MiB file caps, 100000 entries per root, conservative refusals, no rg dependency. Content age uses memory_changed_at with created_at fallback. Merge receipts survive failures; exports stage then rename and regenerate stale indexes. SDK gap: the injected host client asserts pm-extension without an author flag; a native dispatcher adapter clears that fallback and preserves the documented author chain. Focused attribution, 100k URL and bounded streaming regressions pass."
  "2026-10-19T16:14:09.979Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof ledger: 22 targeted regressions fail with the corresponding behavior reverted and pass after restoration. Cases cover URL complexity, the fresh README invocation, matching subjects, surviving merge targets, durable merge receipts, raw-field privacy, canceled slug reuse, semantic age, canceled imports, current export paths/indexes, atomic refusal/failure cleanup, excluded exported evidence, safe gh arguments, reverse collisions, prepare environment precedence, portable null devices, archive/artifact assertions, independent inventory/text search without rg, SDK author precedence, root-remedy text, and formatting-only import timestamps. The 100k adversarial scan runs in a child process; a two-second scan deadline kills the reverted regex, while the fixed scan stays below 500 ms. Synthetic OS hooks prove devNull portability. Restored regression baselines pass; the linked pm runner passed 19 of 19. Full npm execution passed 106 of 106 tests; the first strict coverage attempt exposed two missing export destination branches, now covered by empty-target publication and nonempty-target refusal scenarios. No thresholds changed."
